## Date: 2026-10-17 [​](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/updates/\#date-2026-10-17 "Direct link to Date: 2026-10-17")

### Opening up the in-house search API [​](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/updates/\#opening-up-the-in-house-search-api "Direct link to Opening up the in-house search API")

DeepSeek's web and API search capabilities are powered by our in-house DeepSeek search engine, which reliably handles hundreds of millions of search requests from around the world every day. DeepSeek Search is an AI-native general-purpose search engine that indexes hundreds of billions of web pages, supports multilingual search, and returns highly relevant, authoritative, and timely results in real time. It filters SEO spam, GEO manipulation, and low-quality AIGC through strict detection mechanisms, ensuring authoritative and trustworthy information for users and LLMs. For usage details, see the [Search & Fetch guide](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/search).

### DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 Update [​](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/updates/\#deepseek-v41-flash-1017-update "Direct link to DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 Update")

DeepSeek V4.1 Flash has been upgraded to DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017. The official web and APP models have also been updated to the new version. The API calling method and pricing remain unchanged — simply use `deepseek-flash` to access the latest model.

**Performance–cost Pareto improvement**

Compared with the previous DeepSeek V4.1, the new model delivers substantial improvements across benchmarks:

- HLE (w/o tools): 42.6 (44.0\*)
- Terminal-Bench 4.0: 42.3
- DeepSWE v1.1: 77.0
- ProgramBench: 29.1
- NL2Repo-Bench: 68.2
- Automation-Bench v1.0.6: 60.5
- Agents' Last Exam: 35.4
- Apex Bench v1.1: 72.1
- Chartography (w/tools): 83.0
- BabyVision (w/tools): 92.5
- ZeroBench-main (w/tools): 51.0

\\* Tested only on the pure-text subset of the HLE benchmark set. Terminal-Bench 4.0 was tested with the Claude Code framework, and DeepSWE with the Mini-SWE-V2 framework. ZeroBench-main was evaluated with Pass@5.

